yoyo config get model and yoyo config show no longer hang when .yoyo.toml is a FIFO. The REPL's /config set now refuses one with an error naming the file. Committed as fe78e0da, part of #1047. fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test all passed.

Before and after (fresh dir, mkfifo .yoyo.toml, timeout 5):
• `yoyo config get model`: used to hang until killed (exit 124). Now it exits 0 with the same config file skipped warning that startup prints, and reports the key as unset.
• `yoyo config show`: used to hang (exit 124). Now it exits 0 and prints Failed to read config file .yoyo.toml: … (FIFO). That line now goes to stderr instead of stdout.
• `/config set` and saving an "always allow" choice: the two writers in config.rs would have blocked on the read, and the old empty-default read would then have blocked again on the write into the pipe. They now return an error naming the file and leave the FIFO alone. yoyo config set from the shell already refused with exit 2 (it needs a session), so this fix applies to the REPL.

File sizes: no net lines added to either capped file (config.rs stays at 4851, commands_config.rs at 1993). The new helper read_for_rewrite and its unit tests are in non_regular_read.rs.

Tests:
• tests/config_fifo.rs runs the real binary for config get and config show with a 10-second deadline.
• The near-miss test asserts the exact output model = m  (.yoyo.toml). The task's guess of plain m was wrong; that line is what the binary actually prints.
• The writer tests run on a thread with a timeout.
• I broke each of the three fixes one at a time and each test failed by name, then passed again once restored.
• One mistake along the way: my first writer control hung the test suite instead of failing, because the writer test had no timeout yet. Adding the thread-and-timeout fixed that. The control file was restored and no neutered code remains.

Docs: common-issues.md said config get and config show still hang; I replaced that with what they do now.

Still open, posted on #1047:
• The trusted-dirs store in config_paths.rs (~:299 and ~:326) still uses raw reads; the second has the same read-then-write pattern as config set.
• Upstream #1050 is still open.
• yoyo config show still exits 0 when it can't read the file. I added this to #982 (commands that exit 0 after reporting a failure); fixing it means changing dispatch_sub.rs, which this task didn't touch.
